body:
Recreate the login screen on the user's new wide art: working/classic_ui/hd/login_screen.png. The sheet is 1920x1473 RGBA and belongs to the user (read-only). It holds two pieces:
- the 1920x1080 backdrop at the top;
- below it, at x 10-607 and y 1093-1428, a 598x336 plate: white at about 50% alpha between two red-gold gradient bars.

The plate is the original 332x184 login panel at 1.8x (intermediate_screens/004.png frame 2, as of 2026-11-25).

The user, 2026-11-25:
- "We will also want to recreate the login screen."
- "The font used is the same font the main menu buttons use. The Connect/Cancel buttons have a glow when hovered".

Original layout (screen_login.cpp, as of 2026-11-25). The panel is drawn at UI (99,182) and fades in after 500 ms. Positions inside it, in panel pixels (measured from 004.png):
- the "Log In" title, centred at x 162;
- the "Account" and "Password" labels, right-aligned at x 126;
- the textboxes at (135,40) and (135,63), 147x17;
- three help-text lines from x 57, y about 103-130;
- "Connect" at (41,161) 84x20 and "Cancel" at (217,161) 76x20.

Approved direction: mockup .claude/scratch/coordinator/create_char/login_mockup2.py and login_mockup2.png. Its contents:
- the plate where the original drew it (art 418,328);
- gold small-caps labels in the main menu's font, standing in as Copperplate CC Bold, which ships with the client;
- kit inset fields;
- Connect/Cancel with a glow on hover.

The backdrop follows the HH-0082 cover-fit rule, and positions map through art = 240 + x*1.8, y*1.8. Replaced art is archived to working/archive/.

**Done when:** the screen shows the new art and plate, the labels and buttons match the approved mockup, and hover glows on Connect and Cancel. Login, Cancel, tab and enter all work. It looks right at 4:3 and wide, and both builds are clean.

**Correction, 2026-11-25:** the user: "The glow is white". The Connect/Cancel hover glow is white, not gold. The mockup is updated.

**Correction, 2026-11-25:** the user: the original has a drop shadow, not an outline: "a copy of the drawn text colored black and moved 1px to the [right] and down 1px". The labels use that shadow: black, offset +1,+1 in original pixels (2 art px at 1.8x), with no outline. The mockup is updated (login_mockup2.py). Layout is within 2 art px of the baked panel, and letter-shape overlap is 35-67%, because Copperplate CC is not Copperplate Gothic.

**Approved, 2026-11-25:** the user: "Much better approved" (mockup login_mockup2.py / login_compare.png: drop shadow, white hover glow).

**Verified, 2026-11-25:** review PASS with nits (two rounds); Windows Debug and Linux client builds clean; in client at 4:3: layout matches the approved mockup, typing, tab, Cancel, additive hover glow (faint over the bright plate). Untested: Connect to the server, Enter/Esc, wide/16:9. Remaining nit: the textbox selection highlight does not fade with the plate (cosmetic).
